# Partner package conventions

Applies when editing packages under `libs/partners/<name>/`.

## Layout

```txt
libs/partners/<name>/
├── langchain_<name>/     # Source package
│   ├── __init__.py       # Public exports via __all__
│   ├── _version.py
│   └── ...
├── tests/
│   ├── unit_tests/       # No network calls
│   └── integration_tests/ # Network allowed
├── scripts/
│   ├── check_imports.py
│   ├── check_version.py
│   └── lint_imports.sh
├── Makefile
├── pyproject.toml
└── uv.lock
```

## Exports

- Export public symbols from `__init__.py` with an explicit `__all__` list.
- Import `__version__` from `_version.py`.

```python
from langchain_anthropic._version import __version__
from langchain_anthropic.chat_models import ChatAnthropic

__all__ = ["ChatAnthropic", "__version__"]
```

## Development commands

Run from the partner package directory:

```bash
uv sync --group test
make format
make lint
make test
```

- Unit tests use `--disable-socket` (no network).
- Mirror source structure in `tests/unit_tests/`.
- Do not touch `uv.lock` or add deps without maintainer approval.
